course: dictionary
lesson: 40
title: Acceptance: saying yes and welcoming in
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Acceptance is a noun, and it comes from the verb "accept". To accept something is to agree to take it when it is offered. «We beg your acceptance of this elegant thimble» is a polite way of offering a gift. The words around it show the thimble is being given, so acceptance means taking it.
explain: Acceptance can also mean welcoming someone into a group and treating them as one of you. «Self-acceptance means liking yourself as you are, with strengths and weaknesses.» The clue is liking yourself: self-acceptance means being at peace with who you are, even when you have faults.
explain: Sometimes acceptance means calmly agreeing that something cannot be changed, even when it is sad. Use context to decide which meaning fits. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Then put your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: Acceptance is a noun, and it comes from the verb "accept".
fact: Acceptance can mean agreeing to take something offered, such as a gift, invitation or job.
fact: Acceptance can mean welcoming someone into a group and treating them as one of you.
fact: Acceptance can mean calmly agreeing that something is true or cannot be changed, even if it is sad.
fact: An acceptance letter is a message saying "yes" to an offer or a place.
exercise: In «We beg your acceptance of this elegant thimble», what does acceptance mean? | Losing the thimble | *Agreeing to take the thimble that is offered | Lending the thimble to someone else | Measuring something with the thimble
exercise: What is an acceptance letter? | A letter saying no to a job | A map of the school | A letter about the weather | *A letter saying yes to an offer or a place
exercise: «Self-acceptance means liking yourself as you are, with strengths and weaknesses.» Which phrase best explains self-acceptance? | *Liking yourself, with your strengths and weaknesses | Copying your friends to fit in | Wanting to be someone else | Never making any mistakes
test: Which sentence uses acceptance to mean welcoming someone into a group? | The shop accepted my card for the shoes. | *Everyone in the class included the new boy and treated him as one of them. | He sent back the invitation with a note. | The rain stopped the game at lunchtime.
test: After the bad news, Maya slowly came to terms with it. She calmly accepted that her dog could not be saved. What does acceptance mean here? | Getting a gift from a friend | Winning a prize | *Calmly agreeing that something sad cannot be changed | Refusing to believe anything
exam: Which action shows acceptance of others? | Ignoring someone who sits alone at lunch | Shouting at people who look different from you | Refusing every invitation you are offered | *Sharing your lunch with a new classmate who is different from you
